[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2598491542","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101658#issuecomment-2598491542","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101658","id":2598491542,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a4dWW","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-17T14:29:11Z","updated_at":"2025-01-17T14:29:11Z","body":"> It's always done for export, but with some export plugins `start_run_native` can trigger actions that not involve export (like, starting/stopping server). It's probably still OK to update preset in these cases.\r\n\r\nYeah, it should be harmless: it's just looping over `EditorExportPlugin`s and updating a `Dictionary`.\r\n\r\nHowever, if any actions get values from the preset - even if they don't do an export - it would still be important to update the options overrides. I don't see any cases of that at the moment, but `EditorExportPlatform::run()` is passed the preset, so folks writing code in there are going to assume that the preset has all the correct option values on it.","author_associ